.TH LUS-VERSION 1 "" "Lus" "Lus Manual"
.SH NAME
lus-version \- install, list, and select releases of Lus
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBlus version\fR [list [\-\-remote [channel]] | install request | use request | remove version | which [request]] [\-\-json]
\fBlus\fR +request [arguments]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Installs releases of Lus side by side and selects the one that \fBlus\fR runs.
A project written for an older release keeps running under that release while other projects use a newer one.
The releases live in the Lus home, \fB~/.lus\fR by default, which \fBLUS_HOME\fR changes.
The installers put \fB~/.lus/bin\fR on \fBPATH\fR, where \fBlus\fR is the default release.
.PP
A request names a release.
\fB2.0.3\fR is that exact release.
\fB2.0\fR is the newest installed or published \fB2.0.x\fR.
\fB2\fR is the newest \fB2.x.y\fR.
\fBstable\fR and \fBunstable\fR are the newest releases of the two channels.
The unstable channel holds weekly builds of the development branch.
.PP
The following commands install the newest \fB2.0.x\fR release, make it the default, and print where it is.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
\&lus version install 2.0
\&lus version use 2.0
\&lus version which
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBlus +request\fR runs any command under another installed release.
It must be the first argument.
\fBlus +2.0 test\fR runs the tests of a project under the newest installed \fB2.0.x\fR, whatever the default is.
\fBlus +request\fR never downloads, so a missing release fails with the command that installs it.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
\&lus +2.0 test
\&lus +unstable app.lus
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-json\fR prints one JSON object per command for scripts.
The output, the exit statuses, and the layout of the Lus home are the same in every release from 2.0 on.
The exit status is 0 on success, 1 when a download or a file operation fails, 2 for malformed arguments, 3 when no release matches the request, 4 when a signature or a digest does not verify, and 5 when \fBremove\fR names the default release.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBlus version\fR
Print the version of the running \fBlus\fR.
.TP
\fBlus version list\fR
List the installed releases and mark the default.
\fB\-\-remote\fR lists the published releases of a channel instead.
.TP
\fBlus version install request\fR
Download a release, verify its signature and digest, and install it.
The first release installed becomes the default.
.TP
\fBlus version use request\fR
Make an installed release the default.
.TP
\fBlus version remove version\fR
Delete an installed release.
The default release cannot be removed.
.TP
\fBlus version which [request]\fR
Print the path of the executable of an installed release, by default the default release.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
The command succeeded.
.TP
1
A download or a file operation failed.
.TP
2
The arguments are malformed.
.TP
3
No release matches the request.
.TP
4
A signature or a digest does not verify.
.TP
5
The release that remove names is the default.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lus (1)
.PP
The CLI page of the Lus manual, https://lus.dev/manual/cli#lus-version, has the same text with links to the rest of the manual.
